### Arquivo de Testes HTTP para Autenticação
### Baseado no padrão Aurora Platform
### 
### Este arquivo contém exemplos de requisições HTTP para testar os endpoints de autenticação.
### Use com REST Client (VSCode) ou similar.
###
### Variáveis de ambiente (configure no início do arquivo ou no seu cliente HTTP)
@host = http://localhost:3101
@apiBase = {{host}}/v1
@token = 
@refreshToken = 

### ============================================
### CENÁRIO 1: Login (Rota Pública)
### ============================================

### POST /auth/login - Login com credenciais válidas (200)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

### POST /auth/login - Login com credenciais inválidas (401)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### POST /auth/login - Login sem dados (400)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### ============================================
### CENÁRIO 2: Obter Token de Desenvolvimento (Rota Pública)
### ============================================

### POST /auth/dev-token - Obter token de desenvolvimento (200)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/dev-token
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

### ============================================
### CENÁRIO 3: Refresh Token (Rota Pública)
### ============================================

### POST /auth/refresh - Renovar tokens com refresh token válido (200)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### POST /auth/refresh - Renovar tokens com refresh token inválido (401)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "invalid-refresh-token"
}

### POST /auth/refresh - Renovar tokens sem refresh token (400)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### ============================================
### CENÁRIO 4: Logout (Rota Pública)
### ============================================

### POST /auth/logout - Revogar refresh token (200)
POST {{apiBase}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### ============================================
### CENÁRIO 5: Me (Rota Protegida - Requer Autenticação)
### ============================================

### GET /auth/me - Obter informações do usuário autenticado (200)
GET {{apiBase}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### GET /auth/me - Tentar acessar sem token (401)
GET {{apiBase}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json

### GET /auth/me - Tentar acessar com token inválido (401)
GET {{apiBase}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token

### GET /auth/me - Tentar acessar com token expirado (401)
GET {{apiBase}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwibmFtZSI6IkpvaG4gRG9lIiwiaWF0IjoxNTE2MjM5MDIyLCJleHAiOjE1MTYyMzkwMjJ9.invalid


